{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_12ea4a9761d815c0765fd9fb08e4dadbc95984e948a10978c95757180111e2e4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"vincentkoc/tokenjuice@43a621ab06ef snapshot b841247bdb2e28e8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_080e0574dc2ad78174004c348b2445444139ecf4aa85730511fee70e1ab923cc","slc_3ee2d2a8f439fda660b4d2d06fa8c015c9c3117ceb9afa9010a52d7b2b371142","slc_a9efb0693377eee88a79998a661ba0a6e0cb519dc18192fdf54b18e45ed717a7"],"source_ids":["src_f20f33d559455ba9a3052f838a3bca7c"],"text":"The CLI ships install/uninstall commands covering many agent hosts (including claude-code, codex, cursor, droid, copilot-cli), plus `doctor hooks` to check installed wiring and `doctor <host>` for a single integration.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1b39b28e54f0344981ba85b66ddae5196177e6fed2c9fd316f57c39ace214af2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"vincentkoc/tokenjuice@43a621ab06ef snapshot b841247bdb2e28e8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_07b86ea2a416906796bc94a0ad41e07b71fad9bc09ee7d623815e37869c29895","slc_413df575d10e1115c7816355576a7ac152a1b46c1a455bf5582e071a437f102d","slc_d171ddac132882c206e29982e165d17e8d237bf0d9161450cf5429eeb8c8caf1"],"source_ids":["src_f20f33d559455ba9a3052f838a3bca7c"],"text":"Documented integrations include Claude Code, CodeBuddy, Codex CLI, Cursor, Droid, GitHub Copilot CLI, and OpenClaw, each with an install command and hook/settings file location; OpenClaw support is bundled on the OpenClaw side and requires version 2026.4.22 or newer.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1baf119d122b6de0611f2750b4801eb0a8641396e85f7ac74c4570636c8325f6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"vincentkoc/tokenjuice@43a621ab06ef snapshot b841247bdb2e28e8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3a1f8db37d7a5007401b082d16e983a5547e7e8ba0c21fb9da2152a99f134e25"],"source_ids":["src_f20f33d559455ba9a3052f838a3bca7c"],"text":"Host adapters apply a narrow safe-inventory policy: exact file-content reads stay raw, standalone repository inventory commands can be compacted, and unsafe mixed command sequences stay raw.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2aed415c8051e4b113c13b67c42346d05963b8fe58f50e20418c8295f6c44335","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"vincentkoc/tokenjuice@43a621ab06ef snapshot b841247bdb2e28e8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a9efb0693377eee88a79998a661ba0a6e0cb519dc18192fdf54b18e45ed717a7"],"source_ids":["src_f20f33d559455ba9a3052f838a3bca7c"],"text":"The CLI has three surfaces: `reduce` compacts existing text, `wrap` runs a command and compacts its observed output, and `reduce-json` provides a stable machine protocol for host adapters.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6262ae9de4ca0a4a1de7af14adff2f8b3676b54349a88b1ffff12f6003abc0f4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"vincentkoc/tokenjuice@43a621ab06ef snapshot b841247bdb2e28e8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0c84ea69cef3b1b766505b66021d19660a7a4daeb85c6b667e23509743f79dc9","slc_1de6aa9c4b190666744dfabc33e31277c4895d2a600bb181f03178701b0bfee5","slc_5bbf9ac8175106d4634b7afe3c8165ad2a2e9f6d4090f732dde57215528f4de9","slc_accceee1767aab7a4980fe72e34202a0888270e23cba8a1b5087fbc1037de12b"],"source_ids":["src_f20f33d559455ba9a3052f838a3bca7c"],"text":"tokenjuice is distributed via npm (`npm install -g tokenjuice`), pnpm, yarn global, and a Homebrew tap (`brew tap vincentkoc/tap; brew install tokenjuice`).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6820141872b1c8bab63a6b6b95af564a3f20a45d0b1067f322c30de42590e81f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"vincentkoc/tokenjuice@43a621ab06ef snapshot b841247bdb2e28e8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7780139f350fc6b6f7c25e3869f78da5e01ef9770aa4233049f7b595f6c49476"],"source_ids":["src_f20f33d559455ba9a3052f838a3bca7c"],"text":"The project's stated status is a usable foundation for token reduction with diagnostics and a growing reducer set, now focused on deeper coverage and tuning.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6b1c93925aca75d3c71781f7ffffa0a712075c9edddc351d57440f94fc21e496","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"vincentkoc/tokenjuice@43a621ab06ef snapshot b841247bdb2e28e8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e7dd86da69cd2d99dbfe1c259f1e5f362337a5a0aae3f2561a17964636687251"],"source_ids":["src_f20f33d559455ba9a3052f838a3bca7c"],"text":"Repository development practice: Homebrew publication is owned by the Tokenjuice workflow in the canonical vincentkoc/homebrew-tap repository, and release maintainers dispatch it manually with the published tag until GitHub App automation lands.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_798e8d56af8265e89e755d8d3222777cddce51f50f3fbfb205a6d277e166807e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"vincentkoc/tokenjuice@43a621ab06ef snapshot b841247bdb2e28e8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d2d91249b38d4f07888310041ca8b3e0d125f3dbc309b62f876ac2b5d1c6128a"],"source_ids":["src_f20f33d559455ba9a3052f838a3bca7c"],"text":"Statistics use bounded metadata segments, support paging via --limit and a returned --cursor, report partial coverage, and can be disabled with TOKENJUICE_STATS=off or --no-stats; artifact retention is opt-in via --store.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7d8678b137277b1f3874b1c7d5de25001dad27d72211fcff0b4c49c899459906","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"vincentkoc/tokenjuice@43a621ab06ef snapshot b841247bdb2e28e8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0d88f3b9809142e60cd58354e4cc91419eca2359542b85cdc2a140c775b89270","slc_17000b7e4f2708013bd4f3cb311f362505fef65975544f7923127b3aafdb2511","slc_2c12e8959e08e55c355734a7784639fdb7d0368194ac2a4c917c4fa71471bd47","slc_56348925757679e19099023dcf2ea1ecc80b02f0f21a9124f8a83471efc25a10","slc_6f888e79b6276f7c170495f1cbd244a60db6dc7d40c4f2b6abd071707cf9c72f","slc_73693f663ac711e0d08fdff84a5bd9258963606ad7356119a1f1be6e3a004196","slc_8cc4963334b402241a72cfca15621b67d3f9fc0a3034dd39f54d24e7118143e3","slc_dcb60da43a5d0a77ee0a8fa4dcd501c915c26157ed7aa97bb16f4ad9e5e41e43"],"source_ids":["src_134d2416ccc955769b770492043eceb3","src_379dce5b7b9f5e6fb357e3552fb9afee","src_8a066265cb4f576380d4c9297a97e6b6","src_c862121ded9756e5a1348393ea14fc31","src_fb8a9d1556a75ac1823103cddcd35070"],"text":"Several integrations (AdaL, Aether, Agent Layer, Agentlink) are documented as beta and guidance-only: they write instruction files telling agents to use `tokenjuice wrap`, but do not intercept or replace terminal command output.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8563deaaa301352baa4c73d3913786e76f8ec4a7f11e3a00d0f27e1c028ed95e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"vincentkoc/tokenjuice@43a621ab06ef snapshot b841247bdb2e28e8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_849420ec0596b640e42921ac36d10aea730b5ca0faa9166e2d2659cbefd42c11","slc_ebb4515408a34248d9ba3a1d87572cff2d8757117d14a9b9804685b6691aaedf"],"source_ids":["src_f20f33d559455ba9a3052f838a3bca7c"],"text":"`reduce-json` reads JSON from stdin or a file and always writes JSON to stdout; the documented payload includes fields such as toolName, command, argv, combinedText, and exitCode.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9236783652fb6073241ccd2c6160a2b6df79cef51773d2d8df8258f43f40b27f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"vincentkoc/tokenjuice@43a621ab06ef snapshot b841247bdb2e28e8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c53e6e55b87489118812765b374238ed5487ce5f011f1ff936a451febf5ad979"],"source_ids":["src_f20f33d559455ba9a3052f838a3bca7c"],"text":"tokenjuice is described as a deterministic output compactor for terminal-heavy agent workflows: it observes command output after execution and returns a smaller payload built from rule-driven reducers instead of the full terminal text.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a61f3305173e2669b96b8618c2fcb64b7a5f9cb5f05c4cafdfdbf3a027eaa995","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"vincentkoc/tokenjuice@43a621ab06ef snapshot b841247bdb2e28e8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_424b68ff8abae0e257123ee28bfb935efabf5ddca69d6da6766739b66e1e3670","slc_c53e6e55b87489118812765b374238ed5487ce5f011f1ff936a451febf5ad979"],"source_ids":["src_f20f33d559455ba9a3052f838a3bca7c"],"text":"The design keeps command semantics untouched, exposes raw output only via explicit --raw/--full or opt-in artifact storage, keeps rules as inspectable JSON, and keeps host integrations as thin wrappers around one shared core reducer.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c4076aa8303a4fe2a278b2ee6ba86f0fdb8a1d32183dc38d1d7b2ce591ba1fff","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"vincentkoc/tokenjuice@43a621ab06ef snapshot b841247bdb2e28e8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3a1f8db37d7a5007401b082d16e983a5547e7e8ba0c21fb9da2152a99f134e25"],"source_ids":["src_f20f33d559455ba9a3052f838a3bca7c"],"text":"The reduction engine is rule-driven: built-in JSON rules live in src/rules, user overrides in ~/.config/tokenjuice/rules, and project overrides in .tokenjuice/rules, with later layers overriding earlier ones by rule id.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24"}
